COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[104,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nBegin today a program where you read or listen to stories of the Prophets of Allah, starting with the Messengers of firm resolve.\nShare a message containing a glad tiding of good, and another containing a warning from evil.\nRead or listen to a lecture about the miraculous nature of the Holy Quran.\nguid\nAllah, the Almighty, Has established evidence on people by sending His Messengers and revealing His Books, so no one will have an excuse.\nThis Book (The Holy Quran) has some of Allah's Knowledge for people to be aware of what He likes and what He does not.\nThe disbelievers and transgressors are not guided by Allah except toward one way only which is Hellfire, hence why some people follow and rejoice in imitating them?\nrefl\nرُّسُلٗا مُّبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنذِرِينَ لِئَلَّا يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ حُجَّةُۢ بَعۡدَ ٱلرُّسُلِۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمٗا ١٦٥\n(So that the people may have no excuse before Allah after [the coming of] the messengers): means Allah saying: I have sent my Messengers as bearers of glad tidings and as warners to my servants, lest those who disbelieved in me, worshiped partners or became misguided, when facing my punishment, will not be able to say: (Our Lord, if only You had sent us a messenger so that we would have followed Your verses before being humiliated and disgraced) [20-134]. Al-Tabari: 9/407.\nIn light of this verse, describe the absolute justice of Allah ?\nرُّسُلٗا مُّبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنذِرِينَ لِئَلَّا يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ حُجَّةُۢ بَعۡدَ ٱلرُّسُلِۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمٗا ١٦٥\nIt is clear from this verse that revelation from Allah and sending Messengers are indispensable, for human minds alone will not suffice. Al-Alusi: 6/263.\nCan one rely on his mind rather than Sharia? Explain in light of this verse.\nرُّسُلٗا مُّبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنذِرِينَ لِئَلَّا يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ حُجَّةُۢ بَعۡدَ ٱلرُّسُلِۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمٗا ١٦٥\n(So that the people may have no excuse before Allah after [the coming of] the messengers): this shows that it is not permitted to fight the disbelievers who are not aware of the message of Islam until they are called to it and informed about it. Ibn Taimyah: 2/371.\nWhich comes first: Calling the disbelievers to Islam or fighting them?\nلَّٰكِنِ ٱللَّهُ يَشۡهَدُ بِمَآ أَنزَلَ إِلَيۡكَۖ أَنزَلَهُۥ بِعِلۡمِهِۦۖ\nAta' bin Al-Saib (a prominent scholar) said: I learned recitation of the Holy Quran from Abu AbdulRahman Al-Salami (a prominent Quran teacher), and every time one of us would finish reciting, he would say: \"Now you have received Allah's knowledge, and so no one today is better than you except one who put it into practice,\" then he reads this verse: (He has sent it down with His knowledge). Ibn Kathir: 1/557.\nWhat comes after reciting verses of the Holy Quran?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَصَدُّواْ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ قَدۡ ضَلُّواْ ضَلَٰلَۢا بَعِيدًا ١٦٧\n(Those who disbelieve and avert [people] from the way of Allah), the disbelievers combined their own disbelief with averting others from the path of Allah. This refers to the leaders of disbelief and the proponents of misguidance. (have indeed gone far astray): No misguidance can be greater than that of one who goes astray himself and leads others astray. He carries the burden of the two sins, incurs the two losses, and misses out on guidance twice...(Allah will not forgive them nor guide them to a way ` except the way of Hell). It is not possible for them to be forgiven or guided, because they persisted in transgression and increased in disbelief. Therefore, a seal has been placed on their hearts and the ways of guidance have been barred to them, because of what they have earned. Al-Saadi: 215.\nWho, among the disbelievers, will receive the most severe punishment? why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَظَلَمُواْ لَمۡ يَكُنِ ٱللَّهُ لِيَغۡفِرَ لَهُمۡ وَلَا لِيَهۡدِيَهُمۡ طَرِيقًا ١٦٨\nThose who denied the message of the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ), thus they disbelieved in Allah, and persisted on their disbelief, while knowing the truth, by transgressing against the servants of Allah, envying the Arabs and rejecting Allah's Messenger Muhammad (ﷺ), (Allah will not forgive them): He will not forgive them by letting them go unpunished. Al-Tabari: 9/411.\nAllah denies the disbelievers His forgiveness for reasons. What are they?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَظَلَمُواْ لَمۡ يَكُنِ ٱللَّهُ لِيَغۡفِرَ لَهُمۡ وَلَا لِيَهۡدِيَهُمۡ طَرِيقًا ١٦٨\nAllah denies His forgiveness to the disbelievers to warn them against continuing on their disbelief and transgression. Ibn Ashur: 6/47.\nAllah denies the disbelievers His forgiveness. Why?\nwords\nوَالأَسبَاطِThe Prophets who were descendants of Prophet Jacob (peace be upon him), and were sent to the twelve Israelite tribes"],[105,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nFrom this verse, list three harmful effects of going extreme in Allah's religion.\nThink of an extremist person, then seek refuge with Allah from that.\nshare a message in which you warn against saying prohibited statements.\nguid\nBeware of saying about Allah that which you do not know, as it is the gravest sin\nThe people of faith are humble and submissive to Allah, the Almighty.\nIf you want true guidance and light, then follow the way of Muhammad (ﷺ).\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا تَغۡلُواْ فِي دِينِكُمۡ وَلَا تَقُولُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَقَّۚ\nThey are addressed as \"The people of the Book\", alluding to the fact that they did not adhere to their Book. Ibn Ashur: 6/50.\nWhy are the people of the Book addressed as such, in this verse?\nيَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا تَغۡلُواْ فِي دِينِكُمۡ وَلَا تَقُولُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَقَّۚ\nExtremism in religion is when a follower of a religion exceeds the limits set by his religion. The Jews were commanded to follow the Torah and honor their Messenger, but they exceeded that to resenting other Messengers like Jesus (peace be upon him) and Muhammad (ﷺ). The Christians were commanded to follow and honor Jesus (peace be upon him) but they exceeded that by claiming his divinity while denying the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ). Ibn Ashur: 6/51.\nWhat is extremism in religion?\nوَلَا تَقُولُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَقَّۚ\nThese words imply three things, two of which are prohibitions: it is forbidden to tell lies about Allah and to speak without knowledge about His Names, Attributes, Actions, Religion and Messengers. The third thing is a command, which is to speak the truth in these matters. Al-Saadi: 216.\nThese few words contain great meanings, what are they?\nلَّن يَسۡتَنكِفَ ٱلۡمَسِيحُ أَن يَكُونَ عَبۡدٗا لِّلَّهِ وَلَا ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ ٱلۡمُقَرَّبُونَۚ وَمَن يَسۡتَنكِفۡ عَنۡ عِبَادَتِهِۦ وَيَسۡتَكۡبِرۡ فَسَيَحۡشُرُهُمۡ إِلَيۡهِ جَمِيعٗا ١٧٢\nThe Prophet (r) said: \"He who has, in his heart, an atom's weight of arrogance will not enter Paradise.\" Someone said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man likes to wear beautiful clothes and shoes?\" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Allah is Beautiful and He loves beauty. Arrogance is ridiculing and rejecting the truth and despising people.\"Al-Alusi: 6/293.\nWhat is the definition of arrogance? What is its consequence?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَيُوَفِّيهِمۡ أُجُورَهُمۡ وَيَزِيدُهُم مِّن فَضۡلِهِۦۖ\n(And will increase them out of His bounty): The increase in Paradise entails gardens in which there is that which no eye has seen, no ear has heard, nor has it ever entered the mind of man. Al-Baghawi: 1/627.\nWhat is the multiplication of reward and increase in Paradise?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ قَدۡ جَآءَكُم بُرۡهَٰنٞ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ وَأَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكُمۡ نُورٗا مُّبِينٗا ١٧٤\nThe use of Lordship in, (Your Lord), with the possessive determiner (your) is to show Allah's graciousness to His servants, and indicating that His revelation is for their betterment and refinement. Al-Alusi: 6/295.\nThe use of the term (Your Lord) has a distinctive bearing. What is it?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱعۡتَصَمُواْ بِهِۦ فَسَيُدۡخِلُهُمۡ فِي رَحۡمَةٖ مِّنۡهُ وَفَضۡلٖ وَيَهۡدِيهِمۡ إِلَيۡهِ صِرَٰطٗا مُّسۡتَقِيمٗا ١٧٥\nMeaning: Whoever does not believe in Allah, hold fast to Him and adhere to His Book, Allah will deprive them of His mercy and grace, and leave them to their own devices. Hence, they will not be guided; rather they will go far astray, as a punishment to them for not believing. Thus, all they will gain is doom and loss. Al-Saadi: 217.\nWhat it the punishment of one who does not believe in Allah nor hold fast to Him?\nwords\nلاَ تَغلُواDo not go extreme in your religion\nوَكَلِمَتُهُAllah Created Jesus by His Word that was sent with the angel Gabriel, which is \"Be\" and he was.\nيَستَنكِفَWill never disdain or reject\nبُرهَانٌ(ﷺ)A conclusive proof, who is Muhammad"],[106,"§An-Nisa, Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nExplain to someone the importance of directing questions concerning religious issues to scholars only.\nReview food items that you eat, and keep away from forbidden ones and of doubtful sources because it is harmful to your faith, mind, and body.\nOffer your services today to an Islamic organization or a charitable foundation for helping the needy.\nguid\nA sign of one's good faith is accepting Sharia laws without any objection, and not subjecting the lawful and the unlawful to his own judgement.\nThere is no better way to treat one who disobeyed Allah in dealing with you, than to obey Allah in dealing with him.\nAdapt yourself to cooperate with others in righteousness, but never help anyone in disobeying Allah.\nrefl\nيُبَيِّنُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡ أَن تَضِلُّواْۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمُۢ ١٧٦\n(And Allah is Knowing of all things) means that He Knows the outcomes and benefits of all matters, what is best for His servants and what each relative deserves commensurate with his kinship relation to the deceased. Ibn Kathir: 1/566.\nThis verse concludes with: (And Allah is Knowing of all things). Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَوۡفُواْ بِٱلۡعُقُودِۚ\nOf the Holy Quran, Surat Al-Ma'idah is the most comprehensive with regard to the details of Sharia laws; the lawful and the unlawful, the commands and the interdictions.Ibn Taimyah: 2/391.\nWhat distinguishes Surat Al-Ma'idah from other Surahs of the Holy Quran?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَوۡفُواْ بِٱلۡعُقُودِۚ\nToward the end of Surat An-Nisa, Allah states that when the Jews broke the covenants with him, He prohibited them from good things that were lawful for them. Hence, it is fitting to begin Surat Al-Ma'idah by commanding the believers to fulfill their obligations wholeheartedly. Al-Biqai: 2/384.\nWhat is the link between Surat Al-Nisa and Surat Al-Ma'idah?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَحۡكُمُ مَا يُرِيدُ ١\nAllah ordains what is lawful and what is unlawful, etc; some of which you know the wisdom behind them while others you do not, so seek to learn the wisdom from Him. Al-Biqai: 2/387.\nWhen abiding by the commands of Allah, do you have to know the wisdom behind them? Explain.\nوَلَا يَجۡرِمَنَّكُمۡ شَنَـَٔانُ قَوۡمٍ أَن صَدُّوكُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ أَن تَعۡتَدُواْۘ\nDo not let the hatred of a people lead you to transgress against them for having obstructed you from al-Masjid al-Haram. The above verse was revealed at the conquest of Makkah when the Muslims overpowered the polytheists and wanted to decimate them for preventing them from entering Makkah during the year of Al-Hudaybiyah, but Allah interdicted the Muslims from killing them. Ibn Juzay: 1/223.\nThe importance of justice is clear in this verse. Explain.\nوَتَعَاوَنُواْ عَلَى ٱلۡبِرِّ وَٱلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ\nAl-Mawardi (a prominent scholar) said: Allah recommends cooperating in righteousness and combines it with piety to Him because piety is pleasing to Allah, and righteousness is pleasing to people. So, whoever combines the pleasure of Allah and the pleasure of people would achieve complete happiness and blessing. Al-Qurtubi: 7/269.\nHow does one achieve complete happiness? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَتَعَاوَنُواْ عَلَى ٱلۡبِرِّ وَٱلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ وَلَا تَعَاوَنُواْ عَلَى ٱلۡإِثۡمِ وَٱلۡعُدۡوَٰنِۚ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ٢\n(And cooperate in righteousness and piety), this is a general recommendation. The difference between righteousness and piety is that righteousness is more general than piety. Righteousness is performing duties and recommended deeds, and refraining from the forbidden. Piety, however, is performing duties, but not recommended deeds, and refraining from the forbidden. Hence, Righteousness is more general than piety. Ibn Juzay: 1/223.\nWhat is the difference between righteousness and piety?\nwords\nالكَلاَلَةِOne who died leaving neither descendant nor ascendant as heir\nالقَلاَئِدَGarlands which were put on sacrificial animals\nوَلاَ يَجرِمَنَّكُمDo not let it compel you\nشَنَآنُHatred"],[107,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nStudy the chapter on food from a book in Al-Fiqh (Islamic Law), so you will be aware of what is lawful and what is unlawful to eat. Eating Halal food is essential for answering your supplication.\nIdentify some concerning questions about Islam then ask a scholar about them. The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them), who are among the best of all, used to ask the Prophet (ﷺ).\nBefore eating, remind those around you to say: Bismillah.\nguid\nBe content with what Allah Has ordained as prohibited because it is for your benefit in this life and the Hereafter.\nOrdaining special rules for the time of severe hardship shows one aspect of the greatness and wisdom in the religion of Islam.\nIt is prohibited to innovate in religion, or enact laws that are contrary to laws of Islamic Sharia.\nrefl\nحُرِّمَتۡ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡمَيۡتَةُ وَٱلدَّمُ وَلَحۡمُ ٱلۡخِنزِيرِ وَمَآ أُهِلَّ لِغَيۡرِ ٱللَّهِ بِهِۦ وَٱلۡمُنۡخَنِقَةُ وَٱلۡمَوۡقُوذَةُ وَٱلۡمُتَرَدِّيَةُ وَٱلنَّطِيحَةُ وَمَآ أَكَلَ ٱلسَّبُعُ إِلَّا مَا ذَكَّيۡتُمۡ وَمَا ذُبِحَ عَلَى ٱلنُّصُبِ وَأَن تَسۡتَقۡسِمُواْ بِٱلۡأَزۡلَٰمِۚ\nThe wisdom behind what Allah prohibits is to protect His servants from harm that is present in that which is prohibited, and He may or may not unveil that to His servants. Al-Saadi: 219.\nIs it necessary to know the wisdom behind any act of worship?\nٱلۡيَوۡمَ يَئِسَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن دِينِكُمۡ فَلَا تَخۡشَوۡهُمۡ وَٱخۡشَوۡنِۚ\nAllah, the All-Knowing, says to the believers that there is no excuse for any of you to show harmony with the disbelievers, or to hide your faith from them because now their power is weakened, their resolve is drained, and their dedication is depleted so they despaired of defeating you or alluring you to their religion; for they saw your religion is spreading throughout the land. Al-Biqai: 2/392.\nWhy did the disbelievers despair of defeating Islam?\nٱلۡيَوۡمَ أَكۡمَلۡتُ لَكُمۡ دِينَكُمۡ وَأَتۡمَمۡتُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ نِعۡمَتِي وَرَضِيتُ لَكُمُ ٱلۡإِسۡلَٰمَ دِينٗاۚ\nWhen this verse was revealed, Omar Ibn Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wept, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"What is the matter, Omar?\" He replied: \"I wept because our religion was increasing but now that it has been completed, it will only decrease.\" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"You are right.\" Al-Baghawi: 1/636.\nWhat made Omar (may Allah be pleased with him) weep when he reflected on this verse?\nٱلۡيَوۡمَ أَكۡمَلۡتُ لَكُمۡ دِينَكُمۡ\nThe Quran and Sunnah are completely sufficient with regard to the rulings of Sharia, both the fundamental and incidental. Anyone who claims that for people to learn their beliefs and rulings, must refer to other branches of knowledge apart from knowledge of the Quran and Sunnah, such as \"Islamic philosophy\", is ignorant and his call is false, because it is an implicit claim that Islam cannot be complete without that which he is promoting. This is the worst form of wrongdoing, and is an accusation of ignorance against Allah and His Messenger. Al-Saadi: 220.\nEmphasizing the role of philosophy while belittling the Quran and Sunnah is a sign of religious innovation. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَا عَلَّمۡتُم مِّنَ ٱلۡجَوَارِحِ مُكَلِّبِينَ تُعَلِّمُونَهُنَّ مِمَّا عَلَّمَكُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ\n(Training them as Allah has taught you), the author of Tafseer Al-Kashaf (Al-Zamakhshari) said: The repetition of the derivatives of the Arabic word for (learn) indicates the importance of the source of learning, and the fact that learning should always be from the best and most competent source of knowledge, even if one has to travel far for it. Learning from an incompetent source is a waste of time and a regretful endeavor. Ibn Ashur: 6/115.\nWhat is the consequence of learning from an incompetent source?\nوَمَا عَلَّمۡتُم مِّنَ ٱلۡجَوَارِحِ مُكَلِّبِينَ تُعَلِّمُونَهُنَّ مِمَّا عَلَّمَكُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ فَكُلُواْ مِمَّآ أَمۡسَكۡنَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nThis verse indicates the advantage of a learned person over an ignorant one, since a trained dog has an advantage over an untrained one. Therefore, a scholar has an advantage over others, especially if he practices what he knows. Al-Qurtubi: 7/313.\nIn light of this verse, explain the advantage of learning and knowledge.\nإِذَآ ءَاتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ\nAttributing the dowry to the women proves that the woman owns all of her dowry; it is hers and no one is entitled to any of it, unless she willingly gives it to her husband, guardian or anyone else. Al-Saadi: 222.\nThe verse proves that the woman owns her dowry. Explain.\nwords\nوَالمُنخَنِقَةُAn animal killed by strangling\nوَالمَوقُوذَةُAn animal killed by a violent blow\nوَالمُتَرَدِّيَةُAn animal killed by a head-long fall\nوَالنَّطِيحَةُAn animal killed by the goring of horns"],[108,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nLearn today, in theory and practice, how the Prophet (ﷺ) performed ablution (wudu), ensure to perform ablution for every prayer and be constantly pure to attain the love of Allah.\nVisit a patient, and teach him how to purify himself by making Tayamum.\nIdentify three of the biggest blessings that Allah bestowed upon you, which you feel you have not truly appreciated, and offer gratitude and thanks to Him.\nguid\nOne of the blessings of the religion of Islam is its ease in removing all hardships.\nOffering gratitude and thanks to Allah constantly is a cause for His absolute favors and blessings.\nThe remembrance of Allah's favors helps in observing and keeping His covenants.\nrefl\nمَا يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيَجۡعَلَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّنۡ حَرَجٖ ٦\nHardship means overburden or difficulty. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The religion of Allah is easy.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/229.\nThis verse mentions a quality that Allah loves. What is it?\nوَلَٰكِن يُرِيدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمۡ وَلِيُتِمَّ نِعۡمَتَهُۥ عَلَيۡكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَشۡكُرُونَ ٦\nMuhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qarthi (a prominent scholar) said: \"The completion of His favor is absolving the believers of their sins by performing ablution.\" Al-Baghawi: 1/647.\nHow does the completion of Allah's favor happen to one who performs ablution?\nوَلَٰكِن يُرِيدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمۡ وَلِيُتِمَّ نِعۡمَتَهُۥ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nOutward purification with water or dust is meant to be complementary to inward purification which is attained by affirming the Oneness of Allah (Tawhīd) and sincere repentance. Al-Saadi: 224.\nWhat is meant by completing His favor upon us with purification?\nوَٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nHere, Allah instructs His servants to remember His spiritual and worldly blessings, in their hearts and words, because constant remembering of blessings motivates one to give thanks to Allah, to love Him, and have heartfelt gratitude to Him. This dispels self-admiration with regard to acquiring spiritual blessings, and leads to the increase of the bounty and generosity of Allah. Al-Saadi: 224.\nWhat is the benefit of constantly remembering the blessings of Allah?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ خَبِيرُۢ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ ٨\nMeaning: Allah knows what your hearts conceal of ideas, secrets and passing thoughts; so, beware lest He sees in your hearts that which is not pleasing to Him, or there come out of you that which He dislikes. Al-Saadi: 224.\nWhat is the practical benefit of knowing that Allah is aware of the contents of our hearts?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُونُواْ قَوَّٰمِينَ لِلَّهِ شُهَدَآءَ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۖ وَلَا يَجۡرِمَنَّكُمۡ شَنَـَٔانُ قَوۡمٍ عَلَىٰٓ أَلَّا تَعۡدِلُواْۚ ٱعۡدِلُواْ هُوَ أَقۡرَبُ لِلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ\nTell the truth when you testify without favoring a relative or being unjust to an enemy. Al-Qurtubi: 7/372.\nHow does a believer stand firm for the truth?\nوَلَا يَجۡرِمَنَّكُمۡ شَنَـَٔانُ قَوۡمٍ عَلَىٰٓ أَلَّا تَعۡدِلُواْۚ ٱعۡدِلُواْ هُوَ أَقۡرَبُ لِلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ\nAllah forbids Muslims from being unjust in dealing with the wrongdoers among the disbelievers, despite feeling hatred toward the disbelievers, which Allah ordained. How about a hatred for a Muslim which is based on suspicions or whims? A Muslim is definitely worthier of justice. Ibn Taimyah: 2/456.\nThis verse indicates that being just to others is of a great importance to Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nلاَمَستُمُYou had intercourse with your women\nفَتَيَمَّمُواSeek\nصَعِيدًاSand or dust on top of the earth\nوَلاَ يَجرِمَنَّكُمDo not let it compel you\nشَنَآنُHatred"],[109,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nThink of how many times you were saved by Allah from a disaster or an enemy, then offer your gratitude and thanks to Him.\nGive for charity as a goodly loan to Allah, and be certain of its multiplied reward from the Rich, the Generous.\nDo something that softens your heart such as checking up on an orphan, giving charity to a needy person, or submitting with humility to the words of Allah, so you do not become among those with hardened hearts.\nguid\nEntrust all matters to Allah and rely upon Him. Apply all means but do not rely on them.\nIn order to have Allah with you, you should adhere to the acts of worship mentioned in this verse.\nWhoever belittles the danger of the Jews, should reflect more on the Quran.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَكَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ١٠\nThey are inseparable from Hellfire similar to the companionship of one friend to another. Al-Saadi: 224.\nWhat can be inferred from this expression: (companions of Hellfire)?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ إِذۡ هَمَّ قَوۡمٌ أَن يَبۡسُطُوٓاْ إِلَيۡكُمۡ أَيۡدِيَهُمۡ فَكَفَّ أَيۡدِيَهُمۡ عَنكُمۡۖ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۚ\nAs Allah commands the believers to remember His favors, He commands them to fear Him as the Bestower who can change these favors to affliction and said: (And fear Allah), the King whose retaliation is unbearable because He Has no equivalent. Moreover, Allah warns them that He can empower their enemies over them or subject them to other repercussions. Al-Biqai: 2/410.\nOffering gratitude for Allah's favors entails fearing Him. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَلۡيَتَوَكَّلِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ١١\nThe individual's degree of reliance upon Allah commensurate with his level of faith in Him. Al-Saadi: 224.\nWhen enjoining them to rely upon Him, Allah addressed Muslims as: (the believers), why?\nفَبِمَا نَقۡضِهِم مِّيثَٰقَهُمۡ لَعَنَّٰهُمۡ وَجَعَلۡنَا قُلُوبَهُمۡ قَٰسِيَةٗۖ يُحَرِّفُونَ ٱلۡكَلِمَ عَن مَّوَاضِعِهِۦ وَنَسُواْ حَظّٗا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦۚ\nThis verse combines three fundamental proofs for the indifference of the Jews toward their religion: Their intentional breaking of the covenant, their conceit by misinterpreting words of the Torah, and their forgetfulness due to their carelessness about their religion. Ibn Ashur: 6/144.\nThis verse combines three fundamental proofs for the Jews indifference toward their religion. What are they?\nفَبِمَا نَقۡضِهِم مِّيثَٰقَهُمۡ لَعَنَّٰهُمۡ وَجَعَلۡنَا قُلُوبَهُمۡ قَٰسِيَةٗۖ\nThe hearts of the Jews are harsh and tough, so that no exhortation has any impact on them, and they do not benefit from the signs and warnings; they are not encouraged by the incentive of rewards, nor they are deterred by warnings of the consequences. This is one of the greatest punishments a person may receive when his heart becomes like this, in which a reminder of guidance and goodness will only make him persist in evil. Al-Saadi: 225.\nHow can the hardening of the hearts be a type of punishment?\nيُحَرِّفُونَ ٱلۡكَلِمَ عَن مَّوَاضِعِهِۦ\nDistorting the Torah is by misinterpreting its meaning then passing that on to the public. Al-Qurtubi: 6/116.\nHow did the Jewish scholars distort the Torah?\nوَنَسُواْ حَظّٗا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦۚ\n(And forgot a portion) means that they forgot a useful and uplifting part. (Of what was enjoined upon them) from the Torah by their Prophets: Jesus and those before him (peace be upon them). They neglected it as a careless person would, and they did not go back to it. Ibn Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"One may forget some of his knowledge because of his sin\", then he recited this verse. Al-Biqai: 2/416.\nIt is a sign of danger for one to be occupied by other than what Allah enjoined upon him. Explain.\nwords\nيَبسُطُوا إِلَيكُمThey assault you\nنَقِيبًاA leader of a group\nوَعَزَّرتُمُوهُمYou supported them\nوَنَسُواThey neglected\nحَظًّاA portion"],[110,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nList three acts of worship that Muslims became heedless of, or they have distorted them, in order to know the cause for the differences and enmity among them.\nSay: \"O Allah, we seek protection in Your pleasure from Your anger, and we seek protection in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nSend a message to a Christian person in which you call him to accept Islam using a likable language to him but does not violate our Sharia.\nguid\nA divine way of punishment from Allah against nations is dividing them into hostile warring sects.\nWhoever seeks true guidance, should follow what pleases Allah.\nDialogue with followers of other religions does not mean giving up your established beliefs and fundamentals of faith.\nrefl\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا نَصَٰرَىٰٓ أَخَذۡنَا مِيثَٰقَهُمۡ فَنَسُواْ حَظّٗا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦ فَأَغۡرَيۡنَا بَيۡنَهُمُ ٱلۡعَدَاوَةَ وَٱلۡبَغۡضَآءَ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۚ\nThis is a clear statement that the neglection of Christians to some of what was enjoined upon them became a cause for enmity and hatred, which are forbidden among them. This proves that neglecting to perform a duty leads to committing forbidden acts such as enmity and hatred. Ibn Taimyah: 2/260.\nNeglecting to perform a duty leads to committing forbidden acts. Explain.\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا نَصَٰرَىٰٓ أَخَذۡنَا مِيثَٰقَهُمۡ فَنَسُواْ حَظّٗا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهِۦ\nMeaning: Those who call themselves Christians and followers of Jesus son of Mary, while in fact they are not as they claim; We took from them the covenant and pledges that they would follow the Prophet (ﷺ), aid and honor him and follow his footsteps, and that they would believe in every Prophet whom Allah sent to the people of the earth, but they imitated the Jews, and broke the promises and the pledges. Ibn Kathir: 2/32.\nWhat was the covenant that Allah took upon the Christians?\nفَأَغۡرَيۡنَا بَيۡنَهُمُ ٱلۡعَدَاوَةَ وَٱلۡبَغۡضَآءَ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۚ\nWe planted enmity and hatred between them, and they will remain like this until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, the numerous Christian sects have always been enemies and adversaries of each other, disowning and cursing one another. Each sect among them excommunicates the other sects and does not allow them entrance to its place of worship. Ibn Kathir: 2/32.\nHow does Allah punish the Christians with animosity? What is the extent of it?\nيَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ قَدۡ جَآءَكُمۡ رَسُولُنَا يُبَيِّنُ لَكُمۡ كَثِيرٗا مِّمَّا كُنتُمۡ تُخۡفُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ\nAllah commands them all to believe in Muhammad (ﷺ), and presents them with definitive proof of the truthfulness of his prophethood, which is disclosing to them much of that which they were concealing from the people, even from the common folks within their religion. The fact that the Messenger (ﷺ) brought this great Quran which disclosed what they had been concealing amongst themselves - while he was unlettered and could neither read nor write - is one of the clearest proofs of the truthfulness of his message. Al-Saadi: 226.\nThis verse is a proof of the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ). Explain.\nيَهۡدِي بِهِ ٱللَّهُ مَنِ ٱتَّبَعَ رِضۡوَٰنَهُۥ سُبُلَ ٱلسَّلَٰمِ\nAllah guides thereby the one who strives and is keen to attain His pleasure, and whose intention is good, to ways of peace and safety that will save him from punishment and enable him to reach paradise. This refers to the knowledge of the truth and acting upon it, in general and in detail. Al-Saadi: 226.\nWhat should one do to be guided by the Quran? What is meant by ways of peace?\nقُلۡ فَمَن يَمۡلِكُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيئًا إِنۡ أَرَادَ أَن يُهۡلِكَ ٱلۡمَسِيحَ ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ وَأُمَّهُۥ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗاۗ\nIf the Messiah were a god, as Christians claim, he would have -at least- defended himself, but he could not even defend his mother against death. Since he is powerless to defend his own mother, then he is even less able to defend anyone else. Al-Shawkani: Al-Shamilah: 2/29.\nIn light of this verse, how do you respond to Christians who claim the divinity of Jesus (peace be upon him)?\nيَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُۚ\nThere is no reason for their bewilderment that the Messiah, Jesus son of Mary, was created without a father, for Allah creates whatever He wills. If He wills, He creates a human from a mother and father like all the children of Adam; or if He wills, He creates a human from a father without a mother like Eve (Hawwa'), or from a mother without a father like Jesus, or without a father or a mother like Adam. Al-Saadi: 227.\nIn light of this verse: (He creates what He wills), how do you respond to Christians who claim that the Messiah is a god since he was created without a father?\nwords\nفَأَغرَينَاWe caused\nسُبُلَ السَّلاَمِWays of safety and peace"],[111,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nToday, quit doing a sin on which you have been insisting, and remember that sins are the cause of punishment and ending of favors.\nThink of three special blessings that Allah favored you with, and offer your gratitude and thanks to Him because that entails your love of Allah and modesty to Him.\nIdentify a good deed which you are hesitant to do, or a sin that you are hesitant to quit, then intend to do what pleases Allah, and you will gain easiness and comfort in your life.\nguid\nBeing loved by Allah and becoming an ally of His cannot be attained by claims and wishes, but by true adherence to His commands and doing what pleases Him.\nGiving glad tidings and warning are the mission of Allah's Messengers (peace be upon them), so be sure that you combine these two things when calling others to Allah.\nReliance upon Allah is a cause for easing all matters.\nrefl\nوَقَالَتِ ٱلۡيَهُودُ وَٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰ نَحۡنُ أَبۡنَٰٓؤُاْ ٱللَّهِ وَأَحِبَّٰٓؤُهُۥۚ قُلۡ فَلِمَ يُعَذِّبُكُم بِذُنُوبِكُمۖ\nMeaning: If you claim that you are Allah's children and His beloved ones, then a father does not torment his son, and a loving one does not torment whom he loves, and you admitted that He was tormenting you? Allah says, (Why then does He punish you for your sins): why did He torment those before you and turned them into apes and pigs? (Rather, you are humans just like anyone else He created) like the rest of the children of Adam who are recompensed for good and bad. Al-Baghawi: 1/655.\nThinking of one's self as superior to others is a devil's deceit. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ قَدۡ جَآءَكُمۡ رَسُولُنَا يُبَيِّنُ لَكُمۡ عَلَىٰ فَتۡرَةٖ مِّنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ\nAllah sent Muhammad (ﷺ) after a period of time during which there was no Prophet, clear path, or unchanged religions. Idol worshipping, fire worshipping and cross worshipping flourished during this time. Therefore, the bounty of sending Muhammad (ﷺ) was the perfect bounty at a time when he was needed the most. Evil had filled the earth by then, and tyranny and ignorance had touched all the servants, except a few of those who remained loyal to the true teachings of previous Prophets, such as some Jewish rabbis, Christian priests and Sabian monks. Ibn Kathir: 2/34.\nHumanity was in desperate need for the Message of Muhammad (ﷺ). Explain.\nٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nRemember the favor of Allah upon you in your hearts and words, as remembering it increases your love for Allah and motivates you to worship Him. Al-Saadi: 227.\nAllah often commands us of remembering His favors. Why?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوۡمِهِۦ يَٰقَوۡمِ ٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ إِذۡ جَعَلَ فِيكُمۡ أَنۢبِيَآءَ وَجَعَلَكُم مُّلُوكٗا وَءَاتَىٰكُم مَّا لَمۡ يُؤۡتِ أَحَدٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٠\nAlhasan and Zaid bin Aslam said: \"Whoever has a house, a wife and a domestic servant, is a king.\" This is also said by Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) as narrated in Sahih Muslim. Moreover; it is said, \"Whoever is self-sufficient is a king.\" Al-Qurtubi: 7/393-394.\nWhen can one be described as a king? Are we grateful to Allah for that?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوۡمِهِۦ يَٰقَوۡمِ ٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ إِذۡ جَعَلَ فِيكُمۡ أَنۢبِيَآءَ وَجَعَلَكُم مُّلُوكٗا وَءَاتَىٰكُم مَّا لَمۡ يُؤۡتِ أَحَدٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٠\nMeaning: Allah Has done this for you along with other blessings that favored you above the world at that time, just like a loving one would do for whom he loves, and a father would for his son. Nevertheless, He punished you when you disobeyed; it became clear that commendation and censure are based on obedience and disobedience. Al-Biqai: 2/424.\nWhat are the true causes for meriting Allah's favors and evading His punishment?\nقَالَ رَجُلَانِ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخَافُونَ أَنۡعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِمَا ٱدۡخُلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡبَابَ فَإِذَا دَخَلۡتُمُوهُ فَإِنَّكُمۡ غَٰلِبُونَۚ وَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَتَوَكَّلُوٓاْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ٢٣\n(Who had been favored by Allah): with the true faith or righteousness. (Enter upon them through the gate! Once you enter it, you will surely be victorious): they said to the Israelites: do not be fooled by their giant sizes; for their hearts are fearful of you. Their bodies are huge but their hearts are weak. Al-Qurtubi: 7/396.\nThe children of Israel went from sovereignty and blessings to humility and destitution. Why?\nقَالَ رَجُلَانِ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخَافُونَ أَنۡعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِمَا ٱدۡخُلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡبَابَ فَإِذَا دَخَلۡتُمُوهُ فَإِنَّكُمۡ غَٰلِبُونَۚ وَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَتَوَكَّلُوٓاْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ٢٣\nThe two men concluded their advice by saying, (if you are believers), since doubting what the Messenger says invalidates the faith. Ibn Ashur: 6/165.\nThe two men concluded their advice by saying, (if you are believers). Why?\nwords\nفَترَةٍ(ﷺ)An interval between the Messengers: Jesus (peace be upon him) and Muhammad\nمُلُوكًاYou have sovereignty over your affairs"],[112,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nLearn a story from the Quran and teach it to others, for Allah commands reciting and reflecting on its narrations.\nBecome closer to Allah by giving some of your money to charity.\nShare a message in which you warn against major sins, specially murder, and the fact that its perpetrator would live the rest of his life as a regretful loser.\nguid\nEnvy is a great sin and leads to other major sins.\nThe acceptance of good deeds by Allah is a great favor from Him.\nBeware of the whim of your soul because it eases doing evil and lures you into it.\nrefl\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّا لَن نَّدۡخُلَهَآ أَبَدٗا مَّا دَامُواْ فِيهَا\nThis story provides the clearest evidence of breaking the covenants (by the Israelites). Surat (Al-Ma'idah) begins with the demand to fulfill covenants and contracts, and the affirmation that Allah Has taken a covenant from them clearly in saying, (Allah took a covenant from the Children of Israel). Al-Biqai: 2/428.\nWhat is the link between this story and the beginning of Surat Al-Ma'idah?\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّا لَن نَّدۡخُلَهَآ أَبَدٗا مَّا دَامُواْ فِيهَا فَٱذۡهَبۡ أَنتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَٰتِلَآ إِنَّا هَٰهُنَا قَٰعِدُونَ ٢٤\n(So go, you and your Lord), this reflects excessive disobedience and rudeness expressed in a statement that entails disbelief and disdain of Allah, the Almighty, and His Messenger. Far from it, is what the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: We will never say to you what the Israelites had said to Moses (peace be upon him) but we say: \"Go, you and your Lord, and fight, we are indeed fighters with you.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/231.\nPeople's levels of faith vary at the time of a trial. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّا لَن نَّدۡخُلَهَآ أَبَدٗا مَّا دَامُواْ فِيهَا فَٱذۡهَبۡ أَنتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَٰتِلَآ إِنَّا هَٰهُنَا قَٰعِدُونَ ٢٤\n(Indeed, we are remaining right here), we are not going with you. So, their conduct is similar to that of one who wants eternal happiness merely by claiming to be faithful without validating his claim through actions. Al-Biqai: 2/427.\nAll people may become believers if it was not for trials and tribulations. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَ فَإِنَّهَا مُحَرَّمَةٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡۛ أَرۡبَعِينَ سَنَةٗۛ يَتِيهُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ\nPerhaps the wisdom behind making the punishment lasted for this length of time was that most of those, who had said these things and had not been patient and steadfast; who had become accustomed to the enslavement to their enemies, and had no aspirations that would motivate them to do what would lead to acquiring a high status, would die. Thus, a new generation that would develop aspirations of defeating their enemies and not being enslaved would appear, and they would be far removed from accepting humiliation that poses an impediment to happiness. Al-Saadi: 228.\nWhat is the wisdom behind straying through the land for forty year?\nقَالَ فَإِنَّهَا مُحَرَّمَةٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡۛ أَرۡبَعِينَ سَنَةٗۛ يَتِيهُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ\nThis was a worldly punishment, by means of which Allah may have expiated their sin and warded off a greater punishment. This indicates that punishment for a sin may take the form of the removal of a blessing, or delaying it for a later time. Al-Saadi: 228.\nWhat are the types of punishments for a sin?\nلَئِنۢ بَسَطتَ إِلَيَّ يَدَكَ لِتَقۡتُلَنِي مَآ أَنَا۠ بِبَاسِطٖ يَدِيَ إِلَيۡكَ لِأَقۡتُلَكَۖ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ ٱللَّهَ رَبَّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٨ إِنِّيٓ أُرِيدُ أَن تَبُوٓأَ بِإِثۡمِي وَإِثۡمِكَ فَتَكُونَ مِنۡ أَصۡحَٰبِ ٱلنَّارِۚ وَذَٰلِكَ جَزَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٩\n(I would rather let you bear), you would end up carrying (your sin against me and your own sin), which means that if there is a choice between killing you or being killed by you, then I would prefer that you kill me, thus you would be burdened with two sins. (And thus you will be one of the people of the Fire; such is the recompense of the wrongdoers), this indicates that murder is a major sin and that the one who commits it deserves to enter Hellfire. Al-Saadi: 229.\nWhat is the Islamic rule on killing another person? What does it entail for the perpetrator?\nفَطَوَّعَتۡ لَهُۥ نَفۡسُهُۥ قَتۡلَ أَخِيهِ فَقَتَلَهُۥ فَأَصۡبَحَ مِنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٣٠\n(And his soul permitted to him the murder of his brother), his soul encouraged and lured him into it, and presented the killing of his brother as an easily attainable matter. Al-Qurtubi: 7/416.\nDoes the soul have a role in belittling a sin?\nwords\nفَافرُقJudge (between us)\nيَتِيهُونَStraying (through the land)\nفَلاَ تَأسَDo not grieve\nبَسَطتَStretched\nتَبُوءَ بِإِثمِيYou become burdened with my sin\nيَبحَثُ فِي الأَرضِScratching the ground\nسَوأَةَThe corpse (of his brother)"],[113,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nShare a message about the risk of murder and its great punishment.\nRecall a major sin that you had committed, then repent and ask for Allah's forgiveness since He forgives even bandits when they repent before being caught, then He surely forgives those with lesser sins.\nAsk Allah to make you among those who strive in His cause, either with your wealth, knowledge or life.\nguid\nDo not ever commit an unlawful killing because it is as killing all mankind.\nThe corruption of the Israelites was not caused by ignorance and lack of knowledge, rather it was driven by whims and desire for this life's adornments so they incurred the wrath and curse of Allah.\nIf one could bring this whole worldly life to ransom himself from the punishment on the Day of Judgement, it would not be accepted even though it was the reason for his misguidance in the first place.\nrefl\nمِنۡ أَجۡلِ ذَٰلِكَ كَتَبۡنَا عَلَىٰ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ أَنَّهُۥ مَن قَتَلَ نَفۡسَۢا بِغَيۡرِ نَفۡسٍ أَوۡ فَسَادٖ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَكَأَنَّمَا قَتَلَ ٱلنَّاسَ جَمِيعٗا وَمَنۡ أَحۡيَاهَا فَكَأَنَّمَآ أَحۡيَا ٱلنَّاسَ جَمِيعٗاۚ وَلَقَدۡ جَآءَتۡهُمۡ رُسُلُنَا بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ ثُمَّ إِنَّ كَثِيرٗا مِّنۡهُم بَعۡدَ ذَٰلِكَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ لَمُسۡرِفُونَ ٣٢\nThe Israelites were singled out by this ordinance because the Torah was the first Book in which the prohibition of murder was highly stressed. Nevertheless; they were excessively tyrants and rebellious to the point of killing their Prophets (p). Excessiveness in any matter is going beyond the sufficient or permitted limit with total disregard. It means that they had committed murders excessively without remorse. Al-Alusi: 6/393.\nExcessive killing leads to murdering allies of Allah which incurs His Wrath. Explain.\nأَنَّهُۥ مَن قَتَلَ نَفۡسَۢا بِغَيۡرِ نَفۡسٍ أَوۡ فَسَادٖ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَكَأَنَّمَا قَتَلَ ٱلنَّاسَ جَمِيعٗا\nMujahid (a prominent Quran interpreter) said: \"Allah Has threatened the killer with Hellfire, abiding therein forever, His wrath, His curse and a great punishment.\" The objective of this verse is intensifying the prohibition of murdering a soul so people are deterred from it; and it encourages preserving the human life for which the reward is equivalent to saving all mankind. Ibn Juzay: 1/243.\nWhy is killing a life equal to killing of all mankind? What is the objective of intensifying the prohibition of murdering a soul?\nوَمَنۡ أَحۡيَاهَا فَكَأَنَّمَآ أَحۡيَا ٱلنَّاسَ جَمِيعٗاۚ\nIf a person saves a life - that is, he spares someone's life and does not kill him even though his evil inclination prompts him to do so, but his fear of Allah prevents him from doing that; this is as if he saves all humankind because his fear of Allah prevents him from killing anyone who does not deserve to be killed. Al-Saadi: 229.\nIf one saves a life, it is as if he saves all mankind. Why?\nإِنَّمَا جَزَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ\nMeaning: They wage war against the allies of Allah but Allah expresses that as waging war against Him to honor His allies, just as He expresses that giving to the poor as giving to Him in this verse: (Who is it that will lend to Allah a goodly loan) [2:245], in order to induce compassion for the poor. Al-Qurtubi: 7/435.\nThis verse expresses waging war against the allies of Allah as (those who wage war against Allah), why?\nإِنَّمَا جَزَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَيَسۡعَوۡنَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَسَادًا أَن يُقَتَّلُوٓاْ أَوۡ يُصَلَّبُوٓاْ أَوۡ تُقَطَّعَ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَأَرۡجُلُهُم مِّنۡ خِلَٰفٍ أَوۡ يُنفَوۡاْ مِنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ\nWhen public roads and highways become unsafe for travelling, people will cease to travel, instead, they will remain at home and their trading will come to a halt endangering their livelihood. Therefore, Allah ordains these strict mandatory punishments for bandits.Al-Qurtubi: 7/446.\nAllah ordains strict mandatory punishments for bandits. Why?\nإِنَّمَا جَزَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَيَسۡعَوۡنَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَسَادًا أَن يُقَتَّلُوٓاْ أَوۡ يُصَلَّبُوٓاْ أَوۡ تُقَطَّعَ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَأَرۡجُلُهُم مِّنۡ خِلَٰفٍ أَوۡ يُنفَوۡاْ مِنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ\nAs this is the extent of the seriousness of this crime, it is known that purifying the land of corruptors and making the roads safe from killing, seizing wealth and scaring people, is one of the greatest of good deeds, and it is spreading peace in the land which is in contrast to spreading corruption in the land. Al-Saadi: 230.\nAllah mentions the punishment of those who spread corruption in the land, what about the reward of those who spread peace in the land?\nٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱبۡتَغُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِ ٱلۡوَسِيلَةَ وَجَٰهِدُواْ فِي سَبِيلِهِۦ\nFrom among acts of worship that bring one closer to Him, Allah singles out Jihad in His cause, which means striving to fight the disbelievers with one's wealth, life, views, words, and striving to support the religion of Allah with all means at one's disposal, because this is one of the best acts of worship that bring one closer to Allah. Al-Saadi: 230.\nAmong the means of nearness to Him, Allah singles out Jihad. Why?\nwords\nيُصَلَّبُواTo be crucifiedTo be crucified\nوَابتَغُواSeek\nالوَسِيلَةَA means"],[114,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nIdentify the names of reliable television channels and websites from which you can follow the news, and the names of unreliable and hostile channels to boycott.\nList things to do in order to purify your heart such as pardoning and giving others the benefit of the doubt because true happiness is maintaining a pure heart.\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You to purify my heart.\"\nguid\nReflect on the image of the inhabitants of Hellfire who try desperately to escape, but cannot.\nThe gate of repentance remains open even to one who transgressed against others and hurt them, provided that he is sincere in his repentance and rectifies his wrongs to others.\nEngaging in reforming one's self after repentance is a reason for its acceptance and steadiness.\nrefl\nوَٱلسَّارِقُ وَٱلسَّارِقَةُ فَٱقۡطَعُوٓاْ أَيۡدِيَهُمَا\nIn this verse, the male thief is mentioned before the female while in another verse about fornication, the female fornicator is mentioned before the male. What is the reason for that? The answer is: Men have a greater love for money, while women have greater lustful desire, so each is placed in the right order accordingly. Al-Qurtubi: 7/473.\nIn theft, men are mentioned first while in fornication women are mentioned first. Why?\nفَمَن تَابَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ظُلۡمِهِۦ وَأَصۡلَحَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَتُوبُ عَلَيۡهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ٣٩\nFor a thief to repent, he should regret his actions, cease stealing forever and return what he stole to its rightful owners. Ibn Juzay: 1/236.\nWhat are the conditions of a true repentance for a thief?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرَّسُولُ لَا يَحۡزُنكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يُسَٰرِعُونَ فِي ٱلۡكُفۡرِ\nThe Messenger (ﷺ) was so concerned with people's guidance that he would grieve when someone makes an outward display of faith, then returns to disbelief. Therefore, Allah instructs him not to feel sad or grieved for such people, because they are not worth it; if they are present, they contribute nothing, and if they are absent, no one misses them. Al-Saadi: 231.\nWhy should we not feel grief at one who renounces his faith?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرَّسُولُ لَا يَحۡزُنكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يُسَٰرِعُونَ فِي ٱلۡكُفۡرِ\nRushing to disbelief means displaying its signs at every little occasion with every opportunity, and therefore it is similar to someone who walks rapidly to reach something. Ibn Ashur: 6/198.\nWhat is the meaning of rushing to disbelief?\nيَقُولُونَ إِنۡ أُوتِيتُمۡ هَٰذَا فَخُذُوهُ وَإِن لَّمۡ تُؤۡتَوۡهُ فَٱحۡذَرُواْۚ وَمَن يُرِدِ ٱللَّهُ فِتۡنَتَهُۥ فَلَن تَمۡلِكَ لَهُۥ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيۡـًٔاۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يُرِدِ ٱللَّهُ أَن يُطَهِّرَ قُلُوبَهُمۡۚ\nThis refers to the one whose intention in referring for judgement of Sharia is to follow his desires, and if the verdict is in his favor he will accept it, but if it is not then he will resent it, which is an indication that his heart is not pure. Also, if a person refers his opponent to judgement of Sharia, and he accepts the verdict whether it suits him or not, then this is a sign of the purity of the heart. Al-Saadi: 232.\nIs everyone who seeks the judgement of Sharia truthful? Who is rewarded for doing that?\nوَمَن يُرِدِ ٱللَّهُ فِتۡنَتَهُۥ فَلَن تَمۡلِكَ لَهُۥ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيۡـًٔاۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يُرِدِ ٱللَّهُ أَن يُطَهِّرَ قُلُوبَهُمۡۚ\nThis indicates that the purity of the heart is a means of attaining all that is good, and it is the main reason for every good word and righteous deed. Al-Saadi: 232.\nWhy is the purity of the heart important?\nلَهُمۡ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا خِزۡيٞۖ وَلَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٞ ٤١\n(For them there is disgrace in this world), refers to the hypocrites and Jews. The disgrace of hypocrites is humiliation in public and exposing their hypocrisy. The disgrace of Jews is paying the Jizyah (protection tax) or death, captivity, exile and seeing Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) and his Companions victorious. Al-Baghawi: 1/677.\nThe disgrace of hypocrites and Jews in this world comes in many ways. What are they?\nwords\nنَكَالًاIn recompense\nفِتنَتَهُTo be misguided"],[115,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nStay away, today, from television/radio channels and newspapers that are known to be unreliable and hostile to righteous reformers.\nAsk Allah to guide you to be fair and just in your words, actions and judgement, so that you will gain the love of Allah.\nAscertain your objective from learning the Book of Allah (the Quran) clearly, so that you avoid pretension and false fame.\nguid\nJustice is mandatory for all people, even with the enemies of Allah.\nWhen preaching to Allah, do not fear people but fear Allah, the Lord of people.\nWhen learning the Holy Quran, be sincere to Allah and do not let your objective be gaining worldly interests or the praise of people.\nrefl\nسَمَّٰعُونَ لِلۡكَذِبِ أَكَّٰلُونَ لِلسُّحۡتِۚ\nThe Arabic word used for (unlawful gains) is \"Suht\" which means: Ravage. It is called that because it ravages good deeds and wipes them out, or because it wipes out the dignity of the human being. Al-Qurtubi: 7/485.\nWhy is unlawful gain called \"Suht\"?\nسَمَّٰعُونَ لِلۡكَذِبِ أَكَّٰلُونَ لِلسُّحۡتِۚ\nThis verse describes words that get into their ears and hearts, and food that gets into their mouths and stomachs. This represents feeding the hearts and bodies with the worst sustenance: Lies and Suht (unlawful gain). Ibn Taimyah: 2/475-476.\nThe verse mentions two kinds of sustenance on which the Jews feed. What are they?\nوَٱلرَّبَّٰنِيُّونَ وَٱلۡأَحۡبَارُ بِمَا ٱسۡتُحۡفِظُواْ مِن كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِ وَكَانُواْ عَلَيۡهِ شُهَدَآءَۚ\nThe rabbis (devoted servants of Allah) were the ones who guide people with knowledge gradually. Mujahid said: \"Rabbis are higher than scholars.\" Al-Qurtubi: 7/495.\nHow can a Muslim be a devoted servant of Allah?\nوَٱلرَّبَّٰنِيُّونَ وَٱلۡأَحۡبَارُ بِمَا ٱسۡتُحۡفِظُواْ مِن كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِ وَكَانُواْ عَلَيۡهِ شُهَدَآءَۚ فَلَا تَخۡشَوُاْ ٱلنَّاسَ وَٱخۡشَوۡنِ وَلَا تَشۡتَرُواْ بَِٔايَٰتِي ثَمَنٗا قَلِيلٗاۚ\n(So do not fear people but fear Me, and do not trade My verses for a small price), for then you would be concealing the truth and making falsehood manifest for the sake of insignificant worldly gains. If the scholar is free of these faults, then that is by the help and guidance of Allah and His blessing, because He has focused on acquiring knowledge and teaching people, and he knows that Allah Has entrusted him with protecting the knowledge that He had given him, and be a witness thereto. So, he should fear only his Lord, and not let the fear of people prevent him from doing what is required of him or give precedence to worldly matters over religious matters. Furthermore, the sign of a scholar being doomed is that he is content to being idle and doing anything, and not caring about what he has been entrusted with. He neglects what he has been entrusted with, for he has sold his religious commitment for worldly gains. Al-Saadi: 233.\nIn light of this verse, describe the difference between a devoted scholar and a non-devoted one?\nوَكَتَبۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ فِيهَآ أَنَّ ٱلنَّفۡسَ بِٱلنَّفۡسِ\nA life for a life rule is applied, regardless of whether the killer is a chief of a tribe and his victim is a commoner; whether an old one vs a young one, a wealthy one vs a poor one, an Arab vs non-Arab or a Hashemite vs a Quraishi. All of this to negate what the people used to do during pre-Islam period. Ibn Taimyah: 2/482.\nSecurity cannot be achieved unless justice is applied to all people. Explain.\nوَٱلۡجُرُوحَ قِصَاصٞۚ فَمَن تَصَدَّقَ بِهِۦ فَهُوَ كَفَّارَةٞ لَّهُۥۚ\nAllah makes the charitable waiving of legal retribution against the killer an expiation for the waiver, while implementing legal retribution is not an expiation for him. This indicates that waiving is better for him because the calamity expiates his sins, his patience is greatly rewarded, and he receives a higher rank with Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 2/481.\nWaiving is better than retribution. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَن لَّمۡ يَحۡكُم بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٤٤ وَمَن لَّمۡ يَحۡكُم بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ٤٥ وَمَن لَّمۡ يَحۡكُم بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡفَٰسِقُونَ ٤٧\nFor those who do not judge according to what Allah Has revealed, three different descriptions are used in accordance with three different standings. For their rejection, they are described as \"disbelievers.\" For misplacing the rule of Allah, they are described as \"wrongdoers.\" For deviating from the truth, they are described as \"defiantly disobedient.\" Al-Alusi: 6/430.\nAllah describes those who do not judge according to His Sharia as disbelievers, wrongdoers and defiantly disobedient. Why?\nwords\nلِلسُّحتِUnlawful gains\nالمُقسِطِينَThe just ones\nوَالرَبَّانِيُّونَDevoted servants of Allah\nوَالأَحبَارُJewish scholars"],[116,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nCompete with others, today, in performing a good deed like, being at the front row in a prayer, giving a charity to a needy person, or any other good deed.\nPart with a friend who distracts you from the remembrance of Allah, and replace him with another who draws you closer to Allah, for whoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will give him something much better instead.\nShare a message in which you link a hardship faced by a society to the spread of a sin through it.\nguid\nSharia is a trial from Allah for the people to expose those who accept and those who do not.\nYour lifetime on this earth is short so hasten to do good deeds.\nBeware of the means that are used to convince you of the ideas and values of the Jews and Christians. If Allah Has cautioned His Messenger (ﷺ) against being enticed away by them, then those who are below him must be even more careful.\nrefl\nوَقَفَّيۡنَا عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَٰرِهِم بِعِيسَى ٱبۡنِ مَرۡيَمَ مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ مِنَ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةِۖ وَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ ٱلۡإِنجِيلَ فِيهِ هُدٗى وَنُورٞ وَمُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ مِنَ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةِ وَهُدٗى وَمَوۡعِظَةٗ لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٤٦\nWhat is mentioned here as a praise for Jesus and the Gospel does not include the Christians who denied the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ), and altered the words of the Torah and the Gospel then followed the distorted Scriptures. Ibn Taimyah: 2/485.\nAre current Christians included in the praise for Jesus (peace be upon him) and the Gospel?\nوَأَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَمُهَيۡمِنًا عَلَيۡهِۖ\n(And as a criterion over them), the Quran includes what the previous Scriptures contained, and additional divine instructions and promotion of good morals and attitudes. It is the Book which traces every truth that is mentioned in the previous Scriptures, enjoined it, and provides different approaches to it. It is the Book which contains news of the earlier and later generations. It is the Book which contains judgement and wisdom. Al-Saadi: 234.\nHow is the Holy Quran a criterion over all previous Scriptures?\nفَٱسۡتَبِقُواْ ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِۚ\nThis proves that hasting to perform duties in a timely manner is better than delaying them, which is unanimously agreed upon. Al-Qurtubi: 8/39.\nWhich is better: hasting to perform duties in a timely manner or delaying them?\nفَٱسۡتَبِقُواْ ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِۚ\nThis verse indicates that the individual should hasten to perform the prayer and other acts of worship at the start of their prescribed times, and that he should not limit himself only to that which makes the deed acceptable in the case of prayer and other obligatory acts of worship; rather he should strive to do whatever he is able to of the recommended acts of worship, so as to complete and perfect his deeds and attain the position of being ahead of others. Al-Saadi: 234.\nHow can the servant be ahead of others in good deeds?\nوَأَنِ ٱحۡكُم بَيۡنَهُم بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ وَلَا تَتَّبِعۡ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡ وَٱحۡذَرۡهُمۡ أَن يَفۡتِنُوكَ عَنۢ بَعۡضِ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيۡكَۖ\nAllah prohibited His Messenger (ﷺ) from following the desires of polytheists, Jews and Christians. Also, He cautioned him against being enticed by them away from the truth that Allah Has revealed to him. This includes the prohibition of following the desires of those who opposed the divine Sharia and his Sunnah, even from among the Muslim nation. Ibn Taimyah: 2/494.\nThe verse contains important guidance for every person who holds a position of power. What is it?\nوَأَنِ ٱحۡكُم بَيۡنَهُم بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ وَلَا تَتَّبِعۡ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡ\nMeaning: Do not follow the ideas they promote, and because of which they turned away from what Allah revealed to His Messengers. This is why Allah says, (And do not follow their desires in disregard of the truth that has come to you), do not diverge from the truth that Allah has ordained for you, to the vain desires of these miserable and ignorant people. Ibn Kathir: 2/63.\nAs claimed by these ignorant people, what is the substitute for the rule of Allah?\nوَٱحۡذَرۡهُمۡ أَن يَفۡتِنُوكَ عَنۢ بَعۡضِ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيۡكَۖ\nMeaning: Beware of the Jews, your enemies, lest they distort the truth for you in what they convey to you. Therefore, do not be deceived by them, for they are liars, treacherous and disbelievers. Ibn Kathir: 2/64.\nSeeking advice from Jews and Christians may have dire consequences for Muslims. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nوَقَفَّينَاWe sent in their footsteps\nوَمُهَيمِنًا عَلَيهِAnd as a criterion over them (Scriptures)\nشِرعَةً وَمِنهَاجًاA law and a way of life\nلِيَبلُوَكُمSo that He tests you"],[117,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nAsk Allah repeatedly today to purify and set right your heart.\nPay a visit or give a present to a Muslim who is younger or less fortunate than you.\nShare a message in which you encourage others to boycott anyone who ridicules the religion of Allah.\nguid\nA believer does not take a disbeliever as an ally, and whoever does that, has a weak faith.\nA sign of those with sickness in their hearts is that they hasten to please and seek the approval of the enemies of Muslims.\nThe believer should have an insight to recognize enemies from friends through their words and actions, and not be satisfied with the claims and oaths.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ ٱلۡيَهُودَ وَٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰٓ أَوۡلِيَآءَۘ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٖۚ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّهُم مِّنكُمۡ فَإِنَّهُۥ مِنۡهُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥١\nIt is a known fact that Jews, Christians and hypocrites who live in Muslim societies used to correspond with their religious groups abroad to inform them of Muslims' plans and secrets. In one instance, this resulted in taking a group of Muslims as captives by Mongol Tatars. Ibn Taimyah: 2/496.\nIt is forbidden to take Jews and Christians as allies. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ ٱلۡيَهُودَ وَٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰٓ أَوۡلِيَآءَۘ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٖۚ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّهُم مِّنكُمۡ فَإِنَّهُۥ مِنۡهُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥١\nLove is the essence of alliance, and hatred is the essence of hostility. Love brings harmony and closeness while hatred causes dispersion and conflict. Ibn Taimyah: 2/498.\nWhat is the essence of alliance and that of hostility?\nفَتَرَى ٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ يُسَٰرِعُونَ فِيهِمۡ يَقُولُونَ نَخۡشَىٰٓ أَن تُصِيبَنَا دَآئِرَةٞۚ فَعَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَأۡتِيَ بِٱلۡفَتۡحِ أَوۡ أَمۡرٖ مِّنۡ عِندِهِۦ فَيُصۡبِحُواْ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَسَرُّواْ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ نَٰدِمِينَ ٥٢\n(So you see those with sickness in their hearts) such as doubt, hypocrisy and weakness of faith. They say: We take them as allies now because we may need them (We fear a misfortune may strike us) which means that in case things go in favor of the Jews and Christians, i.e. if they have the upper hand, and we would already be on good terms with them, then they will reward us for that. This is a negative way of thinking of Islam on their part. Allah says in response to their negative way of thinking, (Perhaps Allah will bring about victory) meaning that Allah may cause Islam to prevail. Al-Saadi: 235.\nExplain how negative way of thinking may lead to a great sin.\nفَتَرَى ٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ يُسَٰرِعُونَ فِيهِمۡ يَقُولُونَ نَخۡشَىٰٓ أَن تُصِيبَنَا دَآئِرَةٞۚ فَعَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَأۡتِيَ بِٱلۡفَتۡحِ أَوۡ أَمۡرٖ مِّنۡ عِندِهِۦ فَيُصۡبِحُواْ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَسَرُّواْ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ نَٰدِمِينَ ٥٢\n(Then they will regret) their friendship with the Jews and Christians which did not benefit them or protect them from any harm. Rather, it was nothing but harm, as Allah exposed their true reality to His faithful servants in this life, although they tried to conceal it. When the signs that exposed their hypocrisy were compiled against them, their matter became clear to Allah's faithful servants. So the believers were amazed at these hypocrites who pretended to be believers, swearing to their faithfulness, yet their claims were all lies and deceit. Ibn Kathir: 2/66.\nWhoever chooses to be an ally of the disbelievers, may be punished first in this life. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَن يَرۡتَدَّ مِنكُمۡ عَن دِينِهِۦ فَسَوۡفَ يَأۡتِي ٱللَّهُ بِقَوۡمٖ يُحِبُّهُمۡ وَيُحِبُّونَهُۥٓ أَذِلَّةٍ عَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ\n(They will be humble) due to their compassion and leniency toward the believers, and not humiliation; therefore it is a sign of strength. Al-Biqai: 2/483.\nWhat is meant by being humble toward the believers in this verse?\nأَعِزَّةٍ عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ\nBeing forceful and stern against the enemies of Allah is something that brings one closer to Allah, and is a means by which the person will be in harmony with his Lord in His wrath toward them. The idea of being stern toward them does not mean that we cannot call them to Islam in the manner that is best, thus combining sternness toward them with gentleness in calling them to Islam. Both are in their best interests and will benefit them. Al-Saadi: 236.\nWhen should one be stern against the disbelievers and when should he be gentle?\nذَٰلِكَ فَضۡلُ ٱللَّهِ يُؤۡتِيهِ مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَٱللَّهُ وَٰسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٥٤\nHaving praised them for that which He blessed them with of noble and sublime characteristics, which are indicative of righteous deeds that are not mentioned, Allah then states that this is by His grace and kindness toward them, lest they be filled with self-admiration, and so that they would give thanks to the One Who blessed them with that. Allah, in turn, will bestow more of His grace upon them and others will understand that there is no barrier to the grace of Allah. Al-Saadi: 236.\nThe characteristics of the believers are because of Allah's Grace upon them.\nwords\nيُسَارِعُونَ فِيهِمRushing to the Jews in association\nدَائِرَةٌA misfortune that may strike us\nجَهدَ أَيمَانِهِمThey swore their solemn oaths\nحَبِطَتBecame worthless\nأَذِلَّةٍHumble and compassionate\nلَومَةَ لاَئِمٍA blame of a critic"],[118,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nWhen you hear the caller to prayer, repeat after him then pray for Allah's blessings upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and ask for Allah's bounty.\nGo to the mosque, today, right after you hear the call to prayer.\nShare a message in which you encourage business owners to leave off forbidden gains and cease consuming people's wealth unlawfully .\nguid\nOnly a fool would ridicule the religion and acts of worship.\nJews and Christians hate Muslims because Muslims believe in the Oneness of Allah and all of His Messengers and Books.\nDo not be impressed with the words and actions of the Jews and Christians since most of them are characterized as defiantly disobedient.\nrefl\nوَإِذَا نَادَيۡتُمۡ إِلَى ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱتَّخَذُوهَا هُزُوٗا وَلَعِبٗاۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٥٨\nThe polytheists and disbelievers who opposed Muslims were attacking their religion, mocking it, belittling it, and looking down on it, especially the prayer which is the most prominent characteristic of Muslims and the noblest of their acts of worship. When the Muslims called to prayer, they mocked it because of their immaturity and deep ignorance. Otherwise, if they were reasonable at all, they would have submitted to it and would have realized that it is better than all righteous deeds that a person could do. Al-Saadi: 237.\nDisdaining and mocking religious acts indicate something. What is it?\nوَإِذَا نَادَيۡتُمۡ إِلَى ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱتَّخَذُوهَا هُزُوٗا وَلَعِبٗاۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٥٨\nThe reason for ridiculing the religion is foolishness. Ibn Juzay: 1/242.\nWhat do we learn from this verse?\nوَإِذَا نَادَيۡتُمۡ إِلَى ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱتَّخَذُوهَا هُزُوٗا وَلَعِبٗاۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٥٨\n(That is because they are a people who do not use reason), this holds disdain for them because there is nothing in calling to prayer that entails ridicule; therefore, only silly minded people would do that. Ibn Ashur: 6/242.\nAthan and prayer are of great importance to Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ يَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ هَلۡ تَنقِمُونَ مِنَّآ إِلَّآ أَنۡ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡنَا وَمَآ أُنزِلَ مِن قَبۡلُ وَأَنَّ أَكۡثَرَكُمۡ فَٰسِقُونَ ٥٩\nMeaning: It would make more sense for you, defiantly disobedient, to keep quiet. If you were not defiantly disobedient, which is not the case, and you resented us, it would have been less sinful than resenting us while you are indeed defiantly disobedient. Al-Saadi: 237.\nA sign of foolishness of someone is having two traits. What are they?\nلَوۡلَا يَنۡهَىٰهُمُ ٱلرَّبَّٰنِيُّونَ وَٱلۡأَحۡبَارُ عَن قَوۡلِهِمُ ٱلۡإِثۡمَ وَأَكۡلِهِمُ ٱلسُّحۡتَۚ لَبِئۡسَ مَا كَانُواْ يَصۡنَعُونَ ٦٣\nThis verse is a proof that one who does not forbid evil is like the one who commits it. It delivers a sharp rebuke to scholars who do not enjoin what is good nor forbid what is evil. Al-Qurtubi: 8/81.\nKnowledge alone is not enough, so what should come with it?\nوَقَالَتِ ٱلۡيَهُودُ يَدُ ٱللَّهِ مَغۡلُولَةٌۚ\nIf Allah were to impose blame on the Jews who said that statement and others of their ilk, for some of what they said, they would have been destroyed and doomed in this world. But they say these things, while Allah shows forbearance, overlooks and gives respite, but He never forgets about them. Al-Saadi: 238.\nHow can we infer from this verse the great mercy of Allah, the Almighty?\nكُلَّمَآ أَوۡقَدُواْ نَارٗا لِّلۡحَرۡبِ أَطۡفَأَهَا ٱللَّهُۚ وَيَسۡعَوۡنَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَسَادٗاۚ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ٦٤\nKindling a fire refers to their attempt to start a war, and its extinguishment refers to forsaking them by Allah. This could be a description of their ancestors or those who were at the time of the Prophet (ﷺ) and onward; therefore, this was informing about the unseen and a glad tidings to Muslims. Ibn Juzay: 1/244.\nState briefly an incident where the Jews were forsaken by Allah during the Prophet (ﷺ) time, and another incident during recent times.\nwords\nمَثُوبَةًA penalty\nالطَّاغُوتَEveryone who is worshiped other than Allah\nالسُّحتَUnlawful gains, such as usury and bribery\nمَغلُولَةٌRestrained from doing good"],[119,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nList some causes for provision, which are mentioned in the Quran, and share them in a message.\nWarn against evil, offer advice or explain a religious matter in a clear and pleasant manner.\nRecall a Quranic verse that you memorize but you do not adhere to, then apply what Allah commands you through it.\nguid\nIf you perfectly uphold the religion, Allah will give you the blessings of this life and that of the Hereafter.\nBe certain that Allah protects His allies from what they fear, so entrust all matters to Him to keep you safe.\nOne's faith is true only if he believes in all religious teachings including that which he likes and what he does not. If he believes in what he likes and rejects what he does not like, then he worships his own whims.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّ أَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱتَّقَوۡاْ لَكَفَّرۡنَا عَنۡهُمۡ سَئِّاتِهِمۡ وَلَأَدۡخَلۡنَٰهُمۡ جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٦٥\nThis is by Allah's grace and bounty; having mentioned the evil deeds, faults and false arguments of the People of the Book, He calls them to repent, and tells them that if they believe in Allah, His angels, all of His Books and all of His Messengers, and avoid sin, their bad deeds will be expiated, no matter what they are, and He would admit them to Gardens of Pleasure. Al-Saadi: 238.\nThis verse gives hope to sinful Muslims. Explain.\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّهُمۡ أَقَامُواْ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلَ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡهِم مِّن رَّبِّهِمۡ لَأَكَلُواْ مِن فَوۡقِهِمۡ وَمِن تَحۡتِ أَرۡجُلِهِمۚ\n(And if they had upheld the Torah and the Gospel), upholding them is by learning and practicing. Ibn Juzay: 1/244.\nUpholding the Book of Allah is by two things. What are they?\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّهُمۡ أَقَامُواْ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلَ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡهِم مِّن رَّبِّهِمۡ لَأَكَلُواْ مِن فَوۡقِهِمۡ وَمِن تَحۡتِ أَرۡجُلِهِمۚ\n(From above them and from below their feet) Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) and others said, \"It means: rain and vegetation.\" This indicates that they were in a drought. It is also said, “We would increase their provisions continuously.\" The use of the words (above) and (below) is for showing abundance of provisions. This is similar to this verse, (Whoever fears Allah, He will make a way out for him ` and He will provide for him from where he does not expect) [65:2-3]. Al-Qurtubi: 8/88.\nThis verse provides a remedy for poverty. What is it?\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّهُمۡ أَقَامُواْ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلَ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡهِم مِّن رَّبِّهِمۡ لَأَكَلُواْ مِن فَوۡقِهِمۡ وَمِن تَحۡتِ أَرۡجُلِهِمۚ مِّنۡهُمۡ أُمَّةٞ مُّقۡتَصِدَةٞۖ وَكَثِيرٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ سَآءَ مَا يَعۡمَلُونَ ٦٦\nThis verse indicates that Jewish destitution is due to Allah's wrath upon them because they neglected the Torah and rejected the Gospel and the Quran, which led to the certain divine vengeance against them after the revelation of the Holy Quran. Ibn Ashur: 6/253.\nAllah's wrath evokes destitution. Explain in light of this verse.\n۞يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرَّسُولُ بَلِّغۡ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَۖ وَإِن لَّمۡ تَفۡعَلۡ فَمَا بَلَّغۡتَ رِسَالَتَهُۥۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡصِمُكَ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٦٧\nThis verse is the clearest refutation of the Shias' claim that the Quran is more than what was collected by Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and transcribed by Othman (may Allah be pleased with him), and that the Prophet (ﷺ) had given most of the Quran to Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) who bequeathed it to his descendants. Moreover, they claim that Ali's portion of the Quran was as big as a camel's load and it is hidden with their long awaited Mehdi (the guided one). Ibn Ashur: 6/260.\nThis verse is the clearest refutation of the Shias' claim that the Quran is incomplete. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرَّسُولُ بَلِّغۡ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَۖ وَإِن لَّمۡ تَفۡعَلۡ فَمَا بَلَّغۡتَ رِسَالَتَهُۥۚ\nThis is a confirmation that the Prophet (ﷺ) does not speak out of his own desire, rather he conveys everything he hears through a revelation sent down to him. It also confirms that everything he speaks is revealed to him and not learned from others or deduced by him. Ibn Taimyah: 2/507.\nThis verse proves that the Prophet's (ﷺ) Sunnah is revealed to him by Allah. How?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرَّسُولُ بَلِّغۡ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَۖ وَإِن لَّمۡ تَفۡعَلۡ فَمَا بَلَّغۡتَ رِسَالَتَهُۥۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡصِمُكَ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٦٧\nMeaning: Your duty is only to convey the message, so do not grieve for anyone’s evasion since that is not because of any shortcoming from you, rather it is because of his lack of reason, and Allah Has put a seal upon his heart because He knew that he is not worthy of being guided due to his corrupt nature. Al-Biqai: 2/503.\nState the general meaning of this verse. May Allah enlighten us.\nwords\nمُقتَصِدَةٌOn the right path\nتُقِيمُواUphold and follow\nوَالصَّابِئُونَSabeans"],[120,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you make clear that Allah may forgive every sin except associating partners with Him (shirk).\nRenew your repentance to Allah, and mark today as the beginning of parting with a sin that you were hesitant to quit.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness today as many as seventy times.\nguid\nBeware of conceitedness and wishing to live a longer life because that would turn you away from the path to Allah.\nBeware of associating partners with Allah because it nullifies all good deeds.\nWhen debating non-Muslims, it is allowed to use logical reasoning to prove fallacies in their faith.\nrefl\nوَحَسِبُوٓاْ أَلَّا تَكُونَ فِتۡنَةٞ فَعَمُواْ وَصَمُّواْ ثُمَّ تَابَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ثُمَّ عَمُواْ وَصَمُّواْ كَثِيرٞ مِّنۡهُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ بَصِيرُۢ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ ٧١\nThose whom the covenant was taken from them by Allah thought that He would not test them with hardships because they were deceived by their claim of being Allah’s children and beloved ones. In fact, they were deceived by the long respite. Al-Qurtubi: 8/97.\nWhat caused them not to abide by Allah's command?\nوَحَسِبُوٓاْ أَلَّا تَكُونَ فِتۡنَةٞ فَعَمُواْ وَصَمُّواْ ثُمَّ تَابَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ثُمَّ عَمُواْ وَصَمُّواْ كَثِيرٞ مِّنۡهُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ بَصِيرُۢ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ ٧١\n(Then Allah forgave them), Allah brought the Jews back to truth and obedience. This is an example of the eloquent style of the Holy Quran that attributes this honorable deed to Allah while ascribing blindness and deafness, which are misguidance, to them. Ibn Atiyah: 2/221.\nThis verse shows Allah's Grace to His servants, and their ignorance of what is good for them. Explain.\nلَقَدۡ كَفَرَ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلۡمَسِيحُ ٱبۡنُ مَرۡيَمَۖ وَقَالَ ٱلۡمَسِيحُ يَٰبَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمۡۖ\nAllah states the disbelief of the Christians when they said: (Allah is the Messiah, the son of Mary) on the basis of the specious argument that he was born to a mother without a father, and thus was born in a manner different from the regular ordained manner decreed by Allah. In fact, Jesus (peace be upon him) rejected this claim, and said to them, (O Children of Israel, worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord) thus, he affirmed his total servitude to Allah, and confirmed that his Lord is the Lord of all created beings. Al-Saadi: 240.\nThe statement of Jesus is mentioned after the statement of the Christians. Why?\nأَفَلَا يَتُوبُونَ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَيَسۡتَغۡفِرُونَهُۥۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٧٤\n(Why do they not repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness) shows that repentance is the ceasing of the sins from now onward, returning to the true belief, and seeking forgiveness of the sins of the past and regretting false beliefs. Ibn Ashur: 6/284.\nRepentance and seeking forgiveness are combined in this verse. Why?\nأَفَلَا يَتُوبُونَ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَيَسۡتَغۡفِرُونَهُۥۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٧٤\nAllah forgives the sins of those who repent, even if their sins were to reach the sky, and He bestows mercy upon them by accepting their repentance and replacing their bad deeds with good deeds. The call to repentance begins with a very gentle approach, as Allah says, (Why do they not repent to Allah). Al-Saadi: 240.\nFor one who preach to Allah, how can he benefit from this verse?\nمَّا ٱلۡمَسِيحُ ٱبۡنُ مَرۡيَمَ إِلَّا رَسُولٞ قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِهِ ٱلرُّسُلُ وَأُمُّهُۥ صِدِّيقَةٞۖ كَانَا يَأۡكُلَانِ ٱلطَّعَامَۗ\n(A woman of truth), she was abundantly truthful. It is also said that she was called that because she believed in the signs of her Lord as Allah says, (She firmly believed in the words of her Lord) [66:12]. Al-Baghawi: 1/699.\nMary (o) is called a woman of truth. Why?\nمَّا ٱلۡمَسِيحُ ٱبۡنُ مَرۡيَمَ إِلَّا رَسُولٞ قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِهِ ٱلرُّسُلُ وَأُمُّهُۥ صِدِّيقَةٞۖ كَانَا يَأۡكُلَانِ ٱلطَّعَامَۗ\nThis clearly indicates that they were two weak servants who were in need of the same as all other children of Adam, namely food and drinks, needed. If they had been gods, they would have had no need of food, drinks, or anything else, because the true God is the One Who is independent of means, the Praiseworthy. Al-Saadi: 240.\nThe need for food is a proof that Jesus and his mother, Mary, are not gods. Explain.\nwords\nفِتنَةٌA trial and punishment\nصِدِّيقَةٌAn affirmer of Truth\nلاَ تَغلُواDo not exceed the truth (in your faith)"],[121,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nOffer your thanks to one of those who enjoins what is good and forbids what is evil, and wish him success, even through a message.\nIn a wise and graceful manner, denounce an evil deed today, such as backbiting or gossiping that comes your way.\nBe humble with others today by extending a helping hand, saying nice words, and giving a charity to a weak or a needy person.\nguid\nDisobedience and transgression bring about privation and loss.\nEnjoining good and forbidding evil is an essential part of the religion, and its exclusion by some nations in the past was a cause for them being cursed.\nTaking the disbelievers as allies is a cause for Allah's wrath.\nrefl\nلُعِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِنۢ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ عَلَىٰ لِسَانِ دَاوُۥدَ وَعِيسَى ٱبۡنِ مَرۡيَمَۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَواْ وَّكَانُواْ يَعۡتَدُونَ ٧٨\nTheir affiliation with the message of Moses (peace be upon him), and being the descendants of Israel (Prophet Jacob (peace be upon him)) did not benefit them, for the only beneficial link to Allah is righteousness, specially on the Day of Judgement when close friends will become enemies to one another, except the righteous. Al-Biqai: 2/518.\nJacob (peace be upon him) is a Prophet, yet some of his descendants became disbelievers and were cursed. Does kinship benefit anyone without true faith and worship? Explain.\nكَانُواْ لَا يَتَنَاهَوۡنَ عَن مُّنكَرٖ فَعَلُوهُۚ لَبِئۡسَ مَا كَانُواْ يَفۡعَلُونَ ٧٩\nSome scholars said: It is not conditional for one who forbids evil to be without sins himself, rather sinners should forbid one another from committing evil deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 8/106.\nIs it conditional for one who forbids evil to be without sins himself?\nوَلَوۡ كَانُواْ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلنَّبِيِّ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡهِ مَا ٱتَّخَذُوهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ\nAllah makes clear that faith has essential deeds and opposing ones. It is important to establish the essential deeds and banish the opposing ones. Among the opposing deeds to the faith is taking enemies of Allah and his Messenger (ﷺ) as allies. Ibn Taimyah: 2/521.\nThis verse mentions one of the opposing deeds to the faith. What is it?\nوَلَتَجِدَنَّ أَقۡرَبَهُم مَّوَدَّةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا نَصَٰرَىٰۚ\nThe verse refers to those Christians who accepted Islam, and not all of them because the rest are as hostile to the Muslims as the Jews; they killed Muslims, held them captives, destroyed their land, demolished their Mosques and burned their copies of the Holy Quran. There must not be allegiance nor dignity for them; in fact, this verse is only about those Christians who accepted Islam. Al-Baghawi: 1/702.\nThis verse refers to a certain group of Christians. Who are they?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ مِنۡهُمۡ قِسِّيسِينَ وَرُهۡبَانٗا\n(Among them are priests and monks) means that the ascetic scholars and devoted worshippers in hermitages. Knowledge, asceticism and worship are things that soften the heart and remove the hardness and harshness. Hence the hardness of the Jews and the harshness of polytheists are not found in them. Al-Saadi: 242.\nWhat are the causes of softening the heart?\nوَإِذَا سَمِعُواْ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ تَرَىٰٓ أَعۡيُنَهُمۡ تَفِيضُ مِنَ ٱلدَّمۡعِ مِمَّا عَرَفُواْ مِنَ ٱلۡحَقِّۖ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَآ ءَامَنَّا فَٱكۡتُبۡنَا مَعَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ ٨٣\n(True scholars cry but are not struck insensible, supplicate but do not scream, and become sad but do not fake being unconscious, as Allah says, (Allah has sent down the best message – a consistent Book of repeated lessons – causing the skins of those who fear their Lord to shiver, then their skins and their hearts soften at the remembrance of Allah) [39:23]. Al-Qurtubi: 8/113.\nWhat is the proper interaction with the words of Allah?\nوَإِذَا سَمِعُواْ مَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ تَرَىٰٓ أَعۡيُنَهُمۡ تَفِيضُ مِنَ ٱلدَّمۡعِ مِمَّا عَرَفُواْ مِنَ ٱلۡحَقِّۖ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَآ ءَامَنَّا فَٱكۡتُبۡنَا مَعَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ ٨٣\n(So record us among those who testify), Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: They asked to be among the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) and his Muslim nation. They are the witness nation who testifies to the truth on the Last Day, since Christians are a nation of worship and devotion not a nation of knowledge and testimony. Ibn Taimyah: 2/522.\nWhat is meant by: (So record us among those who testify)?\nwords\nقِسِّيسِينَChristian priests\nوَرُهبَانًاChristian monks\nتَفِيضُTheir eyes overflow with tears"],[122,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nLook for righteous company and try to be with them.\nIf you could not do a good deed today using your wealth or hands, then choose good words to say so that you may be greatly rewarded for them.\nWarn others against a forbidden food item which they are taking lightly, and remind them of a lawful alternative.\nguid\nExpect good from Allah, while hoping for His Mercy.\nConsume only lawful provisions.\nGuard your tongue from making excessive oaths.\nrefl\nفَأَثَٰبَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِمَا قَالُواْ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَاۚ وَذَٰلِكَ جَزَآءُ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٨٥\n(So Allah rewarded them) Allah Has given them (for what they said with gardens under which rivers flow). The reason behind rewarding them for what they said is their sincerity, as Allah says, (Such is the reward of those who do good) which means true believers. Al-Baghawi: 2/704.\nAllah gave them a great reward for what they said. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُحَرِّمُواْ طَيِّبَٰتِ مَآ أَحَلَّ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡ وَلَا تَعۡتَدُوٓاْۚ\nMeaning: Do not exaggerate and make it hard for yourselves by prohibiting the permissible things. Do not transgress the limits by excessively indulging in the permissible matters; only use of it what satisfies your need, and do not fall into extravagance. Hence, Allah's Sharia is moderate between those who go to extreme and those who fall into shortcomings, and it does not allow excessive indulgence nor deprivation. Ibn Kathir: 2/84.\nThis verse indicates moderation in religion. How?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُحَرِّمُواْ طَيِّبَٰتِ مَآ أَحَلَّ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡ وَلَا تَعۡتَدُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ٨٧\nThat is why we should denounce anyone who claims that he will be closer to Allah if he quits enjoying the lawful things. The Prophet (ﷺ) addressed a group of his Companions when one of them said: \"I shall fast and not quit.\" Another one said: \"I shall pray all night and not sleep.\" A third one said: \"I shall not get married.\" And the fourth said: \"I shall not eat meat.\" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: (But I fast and I break my fast, I pray and I sleep, I marry women and eat meat. Whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me). Ibn Taimyah: 2/524.\nWhat is the rule on one claiming that he would be closer to Allah by quitting lawful things?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُحَرِّمُواْ طَيِّبَٰتِ مَآ أَحَلَّ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡ وَلَا تَعۡتَدُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ٨٧\nDo not prohibit the good enjoyable things in life that souls and hearts long for as did the priests and monks who abstained from eating good food or marrying women, and some confined themselves in monasteries while others drifted throughout the land. Hence, Allah reminds the believers not to do the same as those monks did, and not to transgress His limits of both lawful and unlawful things because He does not like those who do so. Al-Tabari: 10/513.\nHow is transgression in lawful things such as eating, drinking and marriage be like?\nوَكُلُواْ مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ حَلَٰلٗا طَيِّبٗاۚ\nMeaning: Eat of the provision that Allah has bestowed upon you and made available by whatever means He has ordained when it is permissible and has not been stolen, usurped or unlawfully obtained. What is permitted is also good, which means it contains nothing impure. Hence, this prohibition includes eating predatory beasts and impurities. Al-Saadi: 242.\nThere are two conditions for food to be considered lawful. What are they?\nفَكَفَّٰرَتُهُۥٓ إِطۡعَامُ عَشَرَةِ مَسَٰكِينَ مِنۡ أَوۡسَطِ مَا تُطۡعِمُونَ أَهۡلِيكُمۡ أَوۡ كِسۡوَتُهُمۡ أَوۡ تَحۡرِيرُ رَقَبَةٖۖ\nThere are three types of expiation for breaking deliberate oaths, and whichever one chooses, it will suffice, according to the consensus of the scholars. Allah mentions the easiest, then the more difficult options, since feeding is easier than giving away clothes, and giving away clothes is easier than freeing a slave. If one is unable to fulfill any of these options, then he fasts for three days for expiation, just as Allah says, (But whosoever cannot afford [that], then he should fast for three days). Ibn Kathir: 2/86.\nWhat is the wisdom in arranging the types of expiation in this order?\nفَٱجۡتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٩٠\nProsperity cannot be attained except by avoiding that which Allah has prohibited, especially the evils mentioned here, which are: Intoxicants which refer to anything that befogs the mind, and gambling which refers to all contests in which both sides offer to give up something if they lose. Al-Saadi: 243.\nHow can prosperity be achieved?\nwords\nوَالمَيسِرُGambling\nوَالأَنصَابُStone alters on which sacrificing was done\nوَالأَزلاَمُThe arrows that the Arabs used in pre-Islamic times as an augury to predict whether a matter was good or evil in order to make a decision about it.\nرِجسٌSinful acts"],[123,"§Al-Ma'idah\ndeeds\nReflect on two of satan's ways to misguide mankind, in the light of these verses.\nSee what is distracting you from the remembrance of Allah and from performing prayer, and eliminate it, so that Allah will substitute for you something much better.\nShare a message in which you warn others against a forbidden food item of which people are heedless.\nguid\nConsuming intoxicants provokes enmity and hatred among drinkers and gamblers, and prevents from remembering Allah and from prayer.\nBeware of disobeying Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ).\nFearing Allah while being unseen by others is of a great importance to Allah.\nrefl\nإِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيۡنَكُمُ ٱلۡعَدَٰوَةَ وَٱلۡبَغۡضَآءَ فِي ٱلۡخَمۡرِ وَٱلۡمَيۡسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ وَعَنِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةِۖ فَهَلۡ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١\nAllah makes clear to His servants that satan only wants to create enmity through intoxicants along with whatever leads to it among the believers, and through gambling, where they used to gamble on wealth and family until the loser became poor and disgruntled, which led to enmity; and if it is not enmity, then hatred which could have unpredictable consequences. Ibn Atiyah: 2/234.\nThe verse warns against things that divide the society and cause insecurity. Explain.\nإِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيۡنَكُمُ ٱلۡعَدَٰوَةَ وَٱلۡبَغۡضَآءَ فِي ٱلۡخَمۡرِ وَٱلۡمَيۡسِرِ\nIntoxicants befog the mind and lead to loss of reason, which in turn leads to resentment between a person and his fellow believers, especially if that is accompanied by trading insults, which is an inevitable result of drinking intoxicants, and it may go as far as murder. In the case of gambling, when one defeats the other and takes much of his wealth for nothing in return, this is one of the greatest causes of enmity and resentment. Al-Saadi: 243.\nHow do enmity and hatred arise among intoxicants drinkers and gamblers?\nإِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيۡنَكُمُ ٱلۡعَدَٰوَةَ وَٱلۡبَغۡضَآءَ فِي ٱلۡخَمۡرِ وَٱلۡمَيۡسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ وَعَنِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةِۖ فَهَلۡ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١\nEvery diversion entices people into more of it, results in enmity and hatred among those involved in it, and prevents them from remembering Allah and from performing prayer, is just as drinking intoxicants. Al-Qurtubi: 8/165.\nWhat are the signs of a prohibited diversion?\nلَيۡسَ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ جُنَاحٞ فِيمَا طَعِمُوٓاْ إِذَا مَا ٱتَّقَواْ وَّءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ ثُمَّ ٱتَّقَواْ وَّءَامَنُواْ ثُمَّ ٱتَّقَواْ وَّأَحۡسَنُواْۚ\nThe mention of fearing Allah when consuming food is an indication that fearing Allah is a noble position. This is utmost inducement to be cautious when consuming food or drinks. The highest level of faith, \"Ihsan,\" cannot be reached without fearing Allah. Al-Biqai: 2/539.\nHow is consuming food related to reaching the highest level of faith, \"Ihsan\"?\nلَيۡسَ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ جُنَاحٞ فِيمَا طَعِمُوٓاْ إِذَا مَا ٱتَّقَواْ وَّءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ ثُمَّ ٱتَّقَواْ وَّءَامَنُواْ ثُمَّ ٱتَّقَواْ وَّأَحۡسَنُواْۚ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٩٣\n(Then they fear Allah and do good, for Allah loves the doers of good), this proves that one who fears Allah and is a doer of good is at a higher rank than a believer who fears Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 8/172.\nThose who are doers of good are at a high rank. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَيَبۡلُوَنَّكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِشَيۡءٖ مِّنَ ٱلصَّيۡدِ تَنَالُهُۥٓ أَيۡدِيكُمۡ وَرِمَاحُكُمۡ لِيَعۡلَمَ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَخَافُهُۥ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِۚ\n(Unseen) is the opposite of the witnessed, and it is mentioned here as a praise for those who fear Allah. They are praised for their sincerity and enlightenment since they demonstrated the fear of Allah without seeing his greatness, his glory, his reward and bliss, but they have ascertained all of that through true inference. Ibn Ashur: 7/40.\nWhy is the word (Unseen) used in this verse?\nلِيَعۡلَمَ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَخَافُهُۥ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِۚ\nWhat matters is the one who fears Him unseen, when no one else is present with him. As for displaying piety and fear of Allah in front of other people, that may be because of fear of people. Al-Saadi: 244.\nWhat is the difference between fearing Allah unseen and fearing Him while in the presence of others?\nwords\nجُنَاحٌA blame\nحُرُمٌWhile on Pilgrimage\nالنَّعَمِLivestock [camels, cows or sheep]\nبَالِغَ الكَعبَةِAn offering to Allah delivered to the Ka'bah\nوَبَالَ أَمرِهِThe consequence of his action"]])